WEBVTT

NOTE Internet Monitor tour: notifications (en). Generated by tools/tutorial/build.cjs.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.598
Notification history lists
every alert the app raised,

2
00:00:03.598 --> 00:00:06.163
where it was sent, and what was held back.

3
00:00:06.163 --> 00:00:10.500
Open it from Notifications in the sidebar,
or from the bell at the top.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.715
Alerts are grouped by day, newest first.

5
00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:17.233
The New label marks the
ones you haven't seen yet.

6
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:21.133
Each alert shows its type,
its time, and a short detail.

7
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:24.633
Here the connection was lost
because every check failed.

8
00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.300
The small tags show where it went.

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.633
A tick means it was sent:
to this computer's desktop, as a sound,

10
00:00:31.633 --> 00:00:35.433
to Telegram, to a webhook,
or to your phone through ntfy.

11
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:39.891
A crossed-out bell means that channel
was held back, with the reason.

12
00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:43.537
This outage happened at night,
so quiet hours kept the desktop

13
00:00:43.537 --> 00:00:47.300
and the sound silent,
while Telegram and the phone still got it.

14
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.716
Other reasons are a channel you turned off,
or an outage shorter than the wait you set.

15
00:00:52.716 --> 00:00:56.233
Held-back alerts are still recorded here,
so nothing is lost.

16
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:01.388
You also see Still offline reminders
during a long outage, speed test results,

17
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:05.167
the weekly summary, and reminders
to follow up on a complaint.

18
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.202
Use the filters to show one type of alert,

19
00:01:08.202 --> 00:01:11.967
or only the ones that were sent,
or only the ones held back.

20
00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:17.295
For example, Held back shows only what
quiet hours or your settings kept quiet.

21
00:01:17.295 --> 00:01:21.100
It's a quick way to check you
didn't miss anything important.

22
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.633
Mark all as read clears the New labels
and the number on the bell at the top.

23
00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:29.893
To choose what is sent where,
set quiet hours, or wait before

24
00:01:29.893 --> 00:01:34.196
alerting about short outages,
open Settings and go to Notifications.

25
00:01:34.196 --> 00:01:37.233
The video tour of Settings
explains each option.

26
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:42.700
Press How this page works on any page to
watch its video. Thanks for watching!
